-- Q25 [Peroxisomes · medium · Skill 2 · ans D] (g23)
WITH q AS (
  INSERT INTO questions (section, topic, subtopic, question_text, options, correct_answer, explanation, difficulty, foundation, content_category, discipline, cognitive_skill, estimated_time_seconds)
  VALUES (
    'bio_biochem', 'The Cell', 'Peroxisomes',
    $qt23$A hepatologist studying a patient's lipid catabolism follows a single \(\text{C}_{26}\) very-long-chain fatty acid as it is first committed to oxidative breakdown inside the cell. The organelle that initiates the chain-shortening of this \(\text{C}_{26}\) substrate before the remaining shortened chain is handed off for further oxidation is most directly identified as which structure?$qt23$,
    $op23$[{"label":"A","text":"The mitochondrion, because it generates ATP by cellular respiration"},{"label":"B","text":"The mitochondrion, because it initiates oxidation of fatty acids of all chain lengths"},{"label":"C","text":"The lysosome, because it carries out acid-hydrolase digestion of fatty acids"},{"label":"D","text":"The peroxisome, because it carries out oxidation reactions that break down fatty acids"}]$op23$::jsonb,
    'D',
    $ex23$This is a Biology question that falls under the content category 'Cell and Tissue Structure (BIO)'. The answer is D because the peroxisome is the organelle that carries out the oxidation reactions that begin breaking down fatty acids, so it initiates the chain-shortening of the very-long-chain \(\text{C}_{26}\) substrate. OpenStax states that peroxisomes "carry out oxidation reactions that break down fatty acids and amino acids" (lines 5508-5509), establishing the peroxisome — not the mitochondrion — as a fatty-acid-oxidizing organelle; the very-long-chain \(\text{C}_{26}\) chain is first shortened in the peroxisome, after which the shortened product is handed off for completion of oxidation in the mitochondrion. Because the question asks where breakdown of the \(\text{C}_{26}\) chain BEGINS, the initiating organelle is the peroxisome. The mitochondrion is the "powerhouse" that makes ATP by cellular respiration using oxygen (lines 5472-5476), a downstream and energy-yielding role, not the initiating one for this oversized substrate. (Choice A) The mitochondrion is correctly described as generating ATP by cellular respiration (lines 5472-5476), but ATP production is not the step that initiates breakdown of an oversized \(\text{C}_{26}\) chain; naming the mitochondrion here is an adjacent-fact trap that substitutes the organelle's energy role for the initiating oxidative-shortening role that the peroxisome performs (lines 5508-5509). (Choice B) This reverses the actual division of labor: it casts the mitochondrion as the initiator of oxidation for fatty acids of "all chain lengths," whereas OpenStax assigns the fatty-acid-oxidation function to peroxisomes (lines 5508-5509). The mitochondrion is described only as making ATP via respiration (lines 5472-5476), so claiming it begins oxidation of the very-long-chain substrate inverts the peroxisome-to-mitochondrion hand-off. (Choice C) Lysosomes are not described as fatty-acid-oxidizing organelles in this section; the structure OpenStax names for oxidation reactions that "break down fatty acids" is the peroxisome (lines 5508-5509). Invoking acid-hydrolase digestion misapplies a different organelle's degradative chemistry to the oxidative chain-shortening at issue, making this a misconception trap. (Choice D) Correct. OpenStax explicitly states peroxisomes "carry out oxidation reactions that break down fatty acids and amino acids" (lines 5508-5509); these single-membrane organelles begin oxidatively shortening the very-long-chain \(\text{C}_{26}\) fatty acid before the truncated chain is passed to the mitochondrion, so the peroxisome is the initiating organelle. This is a Scientific Reasoning and Problem Solving question because you must apply the textbook's assignment of fatty-acid oxidation to peroxisomes to a specific clinical scenario and reason out which organelle BEGINS breakdown of an oversized substrate rather than simply recalling each organelle's headline function.$ex23$,
    'medium', '2A', $cc23$Cell and Tissue Structure (BIO)$cc23$, 'biology', 2, 105
  ) RETURNING id
)
